'Australia is home to many unique animals found nowhere else on Earth. The kangaroo is perhaps the most well-known, using its powerful hind legs to hop across the open plains. Kangaroos carry their young, called joeys, in a pouch until they are old enough to venture out on their own. The koala, another iconic Australian animal, spends most of its life in eucalyptus trees, sleeping up to 18 hours a day. These animals are marsupials, meaning they give birth to very undeveloped young that continue growing outside the womb.','TEXT',
