'Climate change refers to long-term shifts in global temperatures and weather patterns. While natural factors have always influenced the climate, scientific evidence strongly suggests that human activities — particularly the burning of fossil fuels — have accelerated these changes since the Industrial Revolution. The release of greenhouse gases such as carbon dioxide and methane traps heat in the atmosphere, raising temperatures worldwide. This warming causes glaciers to melt, sea levels to rise, and extreme weather events to become more frequent. Communities in low-lying coastal areas and Pacific island nations face the greatest risk from rising seas. Addressing climate change requires international cooperation, with countries agreeing to reduce emissions and transition to renewable energy sources such as solar and wind power.','TEXT',
'PREMIUM','HARD',
'What is the author''s main purpose in writing this passage?','{"A":"To frighten readers about extreme weather","B":"To explain the causes and consequences of climate change and suggest solutions","C":"To argue that renewable energy is too expensive","D":"To tell the story of a Pacific island community"}','{"value":"B"}','The passage explains causes (fossil fuels, greenhouse gases), consequences (rising seas, extreme weather) and solutions (renewable energy, international cooperation).','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
