(gen_random_uuid(),'MULTIPLE_CHOICE',5,'GRAMMAR_PUNCTUATION','Punctuation',5,NULL,NULL,'PREMIUM','HARD',
'Which option punctuates the sentence correctly? "After the storm which lasted three days the town began to recover"','{"A":"After the storm, which lasted three days, the town began to recover.","B":"After the storm which lasted three days, the town began to recover.","C":"After the storm, which lasted three days the town began to recover.","D":"After the storm which lasted three days the town, began to recover."}','{"value":"A"}','The relative clause "which lasted three days" is non-essential and needs commas on both sides. A comma also follows the opening adverbial phrase.','PUBLISHED',NOW(),NULL),
